        "original_id": "7e7b0b85-96f0-5988-9392-573b8b04412c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Films: Arrival, The Town\n- People: Denis Villeneuve, Eric Heisserer, Ted Chiang, Amy Adams, Jeremy Renner, Forest Whitaker, Dan Levine, Shawn Levy, Aaron Ryder, David Linde\n- Roles: director, writer, producer, actor, linguist\n- Awards: Academy Award for Best Supporting Actor, Academy Award for Best Picture nomination\n- Concepts: science fiction film, extraterrestrial craft, translation\n\nFacts:\n- Ted Chiang wrote the 1998 short story \"Story of Your Life,\" which was the basis for the film Arrival.\n- The Town was released in 2010, and Jeremy Renner was nominated for the Academy Award for Best Supporting Actor for his performance in that film.\n- Arrival is a 2016 American science fiction film directed by Denis Villeneuve and written by Eric Heisserer.\n- Arrival stars Amy Adams, Jeremy Renner, and Forest Whitaker.\n- Arrival follows linguist Louise Banks, who is enlisted by the U.S. Army to help translate communications from one of several extraterrestrial craft that have appeared around the world.\n- Dan Levine is best known for producing Arrival.\n- Dan Levine, Shawn Levy, Aaron Ryder, and David Linde received an Academy Award nomination for Best Picture for Arrival.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
